  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 126 PM MDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nSaturday begins the long term period with the dome of high pressure \nmigrating back west over MO/KS with a large section stretching back \nover NM. The proximity of the ridge will keep monsoon moisture at \nthe surface with PWATs still elevated, alongside slower steering \nflow and storm motions. Convection Saturday afternoon will again \nfavor development over the high terrain with secondary convection \nfavoring outflow boundary collisions over nearby highland and valley \nlocations of central and western NM. Any of the stronger storms will \nthreaten locally heavy rainfall and flooding in poorly drained \nareas. \n\nSunday and Monday see a similar pattern to afternoon storms with \nfaster storm motions closer to the Four Corners region thanks to the \nencroaching H5 closed low moving ashore the PacNW Sunday before \nejecting eastward over ID/MT Monday. Tuesday and Wednesday see the \nwestern periphery of the H5 become more dominant over NM. This will \nkeep daily rounds of afternoon storms favoring initiation over the \nhigh terrain with slower storm motions over surrounding lower \nelevations late day and evening.",
